#4604
Large Cavern~
   The river comes to an end here in this large cavern, which must be
three hundred feet in diameter.  The water occupies about half of the 
cavern's total area, with the only visible shore line being a small ledge 
to the south.  There is an indentation in the water at the center of the 
cavern here, with water slowly spinning around it in a gentle whirlpool, 
indicating that the river probably empties through a hole at the bottom
of the cavern.
~
