#4618
Sharp Turn in an Underground River~
   The river curves around here as it runs into a sloped wall, heading
down stream to the east.  Mist sprays up into the air as the water 
impacts against the wall, and drips down from hundreds of small
stalactites on the ceiling.  The humid air is very warm here, making 
the cavern hot and somewhat uncomfortable.  To the north, the river
continues beyond the range of sight.
