#4632
On a Great Underground River~
   This great river's brisk current is strong, but not enough so to 
inhibit travel in either direction.  The water is immensely cold, and 
very clear though the bottom is too far down to see.  The river itself 
reaches to the cavern's midpoint and continues on to the north and 
south.  The area is illuminated in a pale light by a strange, purple 
glowing fungus that covers the walls and ceiling of the cavern.  There 
is a small patch of land to the west.
~
