#4750
Carved-Out Chamber~
   This chamber is about forty feet in diameter and ten feet high.  The room 
has been perfectly carved out of the limestone rock, with glassy smooth 
walls.  It must have taken a greatly skilled group of miners to accomplish 
this feat.  There are two doors in the room, one directly above that looks like 
the backside of a secret or concealed door, and a larger one in the north 
wall.  The northern door is made from a stone that is identical to jade, with 
the texture of marble.  The jade doors only blemish is a very small key hole 
on it's upper left corner.  This chamber is otherwise featureless, and why 
someone would carve out a place like this remains a mystery.
~
46 9 0 0 0 1 255 0
D0
The door is glassy smooth, with no handles or grips of any kind.
~
jade stone door~
