#4807
Small Pool In a Dark Cave~
   A fifteen foot diameter pool of water is nested in a shallow groove of this
thirty foot wide cave.  The pool is only about four feet deep at it's center, 
and appears to be somewhat stagnant.  Water slowly drips into the pool 
from a thin crack along the ceiling of the cave, from which a cool draft 
blows.  Tunnels lead to the west and south from here into darkness.
~
